# 19. FULLY RESPONSIVE DESIGN

The entire website must be fully responsive.

**Desktop: 1440px and above**

- Spacious two-column hero.
- Large premium typography.
- Four-column service grid where appropriate.
- Full desktop navigation.
- Large asymmetric image compositions.
- Multi-column footer.

**Laptop: 1024px–1439px**

- Adjust content widths.
- Reduce typography slightly.
- Maintain two-column layouts when practical.
- Prevent image and text overlap.

**Tablet: 768px–1023px**

- Two-column or carefully stacked layouts.
- Two service cards per row.
- Reduced section padding.
- Responsive navigation.
- Adjust floating cards to prevent collisions.

**Mobile: 320px–767px**

- Single-column layout.
- Compact mobile header.
- Hamburger navigation.
- Hero heading approximately 36–44px depending on viewport.
- Full-width primary CTA.
- Image below hero text.
- Floating image cards repositioned safely.
- Single-column service cards.
- Vertical process timeline.
- Stacked appointment form.
- Easy-to-read opening hours.
- Full-width contact CTA.
- Stacked footer columns.

Critical mobile requirements:

- No horizontal scrolling.
- No clipped text.
- No overlapping elements.
- No oversized images.
- No broken grids.
- No tiny buttons.
- Minimum comfortable touch target around 44px.
- Proper spacing around all interactive elements.

Test the website at 320px, 375px, 430px, 768px, 1024px, 1280px, and 1440px widths.

